  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multi-profile + avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best setup so far, and it uses PCA-2000 — the only RNA encoder tested. Image-only (config_010, acc=0.208) is far weaker, so the RNA branch dominates. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether a learned encoder (scvi_n200, scgpt) can outperform the simple linear PCA-2000 representation. This is a fundamental design axis that, if it matters, would reshape the entire search. What this tests: config_005 is a clean single-variable comparison to config_002 (same multi-profile, same avgpool aggregation; only PCA-2000 → scvi_n200). It directly measures whether a nonlinear, learned embedding captures cell-type structure that PCA misses. Why best next: With only 4 experiments done, the encoder choice is the largest unexplored dimension on the dominant modality. If scvi_n200 improves substantially, we know to prioritize encoder selection before investing in fusion; if it does not, we can confidently fix PCA-2000 and shift budget toward multimodal fusion experiments. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about a high-leverage design decision."
}

